  questionText: Which one of the following substances is formed when Mohr's salt
    is infinitely diluted?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: When water is infinitely added to Mohr's salt, a compound known
    as hexaaquairon(II) ion with the chemical formula, [Fe(H<sub>2< sub>O)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>2+</sup>,
    is formed.
  options:
